{#- v3 base layout (overhaul v3, phase A foundation, 2026-10-29). Owner: WS1 (engineering 6).
    Pages not yet converted keep layouts/v2.njk or their old layout; nothing here changes them.

    Head order: charset, viewport (viewport-fit=cover for the call bar's safe area), title, the
    consent-first GA4 block (head/ga4.njk: consent default, then config, then the async tag),
    font preloads (Barlow Condensed 300 and Poppins 400 only, art direction 1.1), the one hero
    image preload (storefront mode only), the hashed core CSS and any page bundle CSS, the hashed
    core JS (deferred) and page bundle JS, then robots (exactly one), description, canonical,
    Open Graph and Twitter, icons, JSON-LD, Clarity.

    Body: skip link first (first focusable), the 8px top sentinel the header observer watches, the
    header, the phone call bar, the cookie bar (both fixed; moved up in peak pass R2), <main
    id="main">, the footer, the #bc-hours config block (one per page, read by the action system).
    Critical CSS: .eleventy.js inlines the page's matching rules and loads the hashed sheets
    without blocking (peak pass R2); the links printed below are what it rewrites.

    Front matter and page data this layout reads:
      page_key          wording key: pages[page_key].meta.title / .description / .image_alt
      meta_title, meta_description   fallbacks when a page has no page_key (internal pages)
      slug              canonical path (index = site root) and frame[slug] (gsv on the homepage)
      og_image, og_image_width, og_image_height   Open Graph image, path under the site root
      robots_noindex    true = this page alone is noindex, nofollow and sends no analytics
      theme or mood     "warm" = Warm Gallery (body.mood-warm); default Showroom Black (mood-dark)
      body_class        extra body classes
      header_raised     true = header raised layer on from load (art direction 4 rule 5)
      hero              the hero slot object (v3/hero.njk): mode "ramp" (default) or "storefront"
                        with image and sizes; storefront mode adds the image preload here
      bundles           page bundles to add, e.g. ["builder"] (assets/v3/css/builder/, js/builder/)
      schema_ld         JSON-LD object built in the page's .11tydata.js (lib/schema.js)
    Globals (WS1, lib/platform.js): noindex (BC_NOINDEX=1, or a Netlify CONTEXT that is set and is
    not production; prints exactly one robots meta, noindex, nofollow), analytics (true only in a
    production build; head/ga4.njk and head/clarity.njk are stubbed otherwise), buildEnv (the whole
    answer), price_mode (printed on <html data-price-mode>), assetsHash (the hashed bundle paths,
    .eleventy.js). A page with robots_noindex is noindex, sends no analytics and prints no
    canonical tag. -#}
{%- from "v3/media.njk" import preload -%}
{%- set noindex = noindex or robots_noindex -%}
{%- set fr = frame[slug] or {} -%}
{%- set m = (pages[page_key].meta if (page_key and pages[page_key] and pages[page_key].meta) else {}) -%}
{%- set metaTitle = m.title or meta_title or site.name_html -%}
{%- set metaDesc = m.description or meta_description or "" -%}
{#- canonical path: the same function the sitemap uses (lib/filters.js canonicalPath), so the two cannot disagree -#}
{%- set url = site.origin + (page.url | canonicalPath) -%}
{%- set heroMode = "photo" if (hero and hero.mode == "photo" and hero.image) else ("storefront" if (hero and hero.mode == "storefront" and hero.image) else "ramp") -%}
{%- set moodName = "warm" if (theme == "warm" or mood == "warm") else "dark" -%}
{#- Link previews (peak pass R1, technical 10): a page with no photo of its own used to share
    logo.png (1612 x 600), which every platform crops. It now shares the 1200 x 630 storefront crop
    built by scripts/images.js, with its own size and alt (global og_share, lib/eleventy-og.js). -#}
{%- set ogShare = og_share or null -%}
{#- Peak pass R2 (technical 10): a page whose own og_image carries no width and height (the 9 gallery
    pages' 4:3 job photos, the builder's old-site 1200 x 540 raster) shares the sized 1.91:1 image too,
    so no preview crops it or fetches it late. Pages with a sized photo of their own keep it. -#}
{%- set useShare = ogShare and ((not og_image) or og_image == "logo.png" or (not og_image_width)) -%}
{%- set ogImg = ogShare.path if useShare else og_image -%}
{%- set ogW = ogShare.width if useShare else og_image_width -%}
{%- set ogH = ogShare.height if useShare else og_image_height -%}
{%- set ogAlt = ogShare.alt if useShare else m.image_alt -%}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-price-mode="{{ price_mode }}">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#0B0B0C">
<title>{{ metaTitle | fill | safe }}</title>
{% include "head/ga4.njk" %}
<link rel="preload" href="/assets/v3/fonts/barlow-condensed-v5.3.0-latin-300-normal.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="/assets/v3/fonts/poppins-v5.3.0-latin-400-normal.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
{% if heroMode == "storefront" or heroMode == "photo" %}{{ preload(hero.image, hero.sizes) }}
{% endif %}{% if assetsHash.css.core %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ assetsHash.css.core }}">
{% endif %}{% for b in bundles %}{% if assetsHash.css[b] %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ assetsHash.css[b] }}">
{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if assetsHash.js.core %}<script src="{{ assetsHash.js.core }}" defer></script>
{% endif %}{% for b in bundles %}{% if assetsHash.js[b] %}<script src="{{ assetsHash.js[b] }}" defer></script>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}<meta name="robots" content="{% if noindex %}noindex, nofollow{% else %}index, follow{% endif %}">
{% if fr.gsv %}<meta name="google-site-verification" content="{{ site.google_site_verification | safe }}" />
{% endif %}{% if metaDesc %}<meta name="description" content="{{ metaDesc | fill | safe }}">
{% endif %}{% if not robots_noindex %}<link rel="canonical" href="{{ url | safe }}">
{% endif %}
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:site_name" content="{% if fr.og_site_name_raw %}{{ site.name | safe }}{% else %}{{ site.name_html | safe }}{% endif %}">
<meta property="og:locale" content="en_US">
<meta property="og:title" content="{{ metaTitle | fill | safe }}">
{% if metaDesc %}<meta property="og:description" content="{{ metaDesc | fill | safe }}">
{% endif %}<meta property="og:url" content="{{ url | safe }}">
{% if ogImg %}<meta property="og:image" content="{{ site.origin | safe }}/{{ ogImg | safe }}">
{% if ogW %}<meta property="og:image:width" content="{{ ogW | safe }}">
<meta property="og:image:height" content="{{ ogH | safe }}">
{% endif %}{% if ogAlt %}<meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ ogAlt | safe }}">
{% endif %}<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ site.origin | safe }}/{{ ogImg | safe }}">
{% endif %}<meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ metaTitle | fill | safe }}">
{% if metaDesc %}<meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ metaDesc | fill | safe }}">
{% endif %}{% include "head/icons.njk" %}
{% if schema_ld %}{% set ld = schema_ld %}{% include "jsonld.njk" %}
{% endif %}{% include "head/clarity.njk" %}
</head>
<body class="v3 mood-{{ moodName }} hero-{{ heroMode }}{% if body_class %} {{ body_class }}{% endif %}">
{% include "skip-link.njk" %}
<div class="v3-top-sentinel" data-top-sentinel aria-hidden="true"></div>
{% include "v3/header.njk" %}
{#- Peak pass R2 part A (technical 2): the phone call bar and the cookie bar come right after the
    header, not after the footer. Both are position: fixed, so nothing moves on screen; what changes
    is that they are parsed (and painted) with the first frame instead of after the whole page and
    any in-body stylesheet (the talk block's book.css). Keyboard order: skip link, header, call bar,
    cookie choices, then main; the skip link still jumps straight to main. -#}
{% include "v3/sticky-bar.njk" %}
{% include "v3/cookie-bar.njk" %}
<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
{{ content | safe }}
</main>
{% include "v3/footer.njk" %}
{%- set statusLabels = (pages.shared.v3.status if (pages.shared.v3 and pages.shared.v3.status) else pages.shared.v2.status) %}
{%- set hoursCfg = {
  "tz": site.hours.timezone or "America/Los_Angeles",
  "days": site.hours.days,
  "opens": site.hours.opens,
  "closes": site.hours.closes,
  "closures": site.closures or [],
  "unknown": site.hours_unknown or [],
  "texts_confirmed": site.texts_confirmed or false,
  "labels": statusLabels
} %}
<script type="application/json" id="bc-hours">{{ hoursCfg | jsonld | replace("<", "\\u003c") | safe }}</script>
</body>
</html>
